\description{
Constructs a NIMBLE model specification for insect biomass, diversity, or
both responses. The model supports continuous and categorical covariates,
optional year, locality, and replicate random effects, and optional temporal
effects. When both responses are included, fixed effects, enabled random
effects, and temporal parameters are shared between the biomass and diversity
linear predictors. Response-specific intercepts and observation-model
parameters remain separate.
}
\details{
The function assembles a NIMBLE model as text, writes the model to an R
file, and invisibly returns the model specification and associated metadata.

When `response = "both"`, the biomass and diversity predictors use the same
coefficients for continuous covariates and the same categorical covariate
effect vectors. Enabled year, locality, and replicate random effects are
also shared. The linear temporal coefficients or cyclic spline coefficient
vector and smoothing precision are shared between the two predictors.
Biomass and diversity retain separate intercepts and response-specific
observation distributions and parameters.

For `temporal_effect = "linear"`, the temporal contribution is

\deqn{
  f(t_i) = \beta_t t_i + \beta_{t^2} t_i^2,
}

where `temporal` is the temporal variable in the generated NIMBLE model.

For `temporal_effect = "cubic_cyclic"`, the function symmetrises the penalty
matrix, performs an eigen-decomposition, and retains eigenvalues greater
than `temporal_penalty_tol` times the largest eigenvalue. The supplied basis
is rotated into the retained penalized eigenbasis. The spline coefficients
have zero-mean normal priors with precisions given by the shared smoothing
precision multiplied by the retained penalty eigenvalues.

The generated model expects the required NIMBLE data, dimensions, indices,
and constants to be supplied when the model is instantiated. Continuous
covariates are represented by `X`, and the temporal variable is named
`temporal`. When enabled, random-effect indices include `year_id`,
`locality_id`, and `replicate_id`.

For the cyclic spline, the returned `temporal_constants` list contains the
penalized temporal basis matrix, retained penalty eigenvalues, and number
of retained basis functions. These objects should be supplied as NIMBLE
constants.

Although spatial-effect options and spatial prior arguments are validated,
this implementation does not generate spatial model terms. Check the
generated model before using non-default spatial options.
}
